s":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-01","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-07","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-08","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"8.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Investment Advisory Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://cds.sevenoaks.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Planning enforcement costs \u00a367k above budget to date with funding mechanism subject to continuous review.","lead":"Material unplanned costs with undefined funding source; forecast may rely on unidentified savings that may not materialise.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Unfunded business rates liabilities on investment properties and loss of CATS property revenue.","lead":"Unfunded liabilities on investment properties create budget exposure; rental shortfalls add to cumulative revenue pressures.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Bradbourne car park income declining by \u00a360k (10% of annual budget) due to new competing facility opened May 2026.","lead":"Permanent structural loss of key income stream from market competition; creates revenue pressure requiring compensating savings or increased borrowing.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","headline":"Planning enforcement costs \u00a367k above budget to date with funding mechanism subject to continuous review.","detail":"Planning enforcement spending reached \u00a3194k actual to end of July against \u00a3127k budgeted (\u00a367k overspend). Full-year forecast shows \u00a3127k (on budget), implying a \u00a367k recovery must be achieved over the remaining eight months. Council notes funding option is subject to continuous review, indicating the mechanism for covering this cost has not been finalized.","category":"other","matters":"Material unplanned costs with undefined funding source; forecast may rely on unidentified savings that may not materialise.","figures":"Planning Enforcement: \u00a3194k actual vs \u00a3127k budget to date; full-year forecast \u00a3127k","quote":"Ongoing costs of planning and legal action. Funding option subject to continuous review.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","headline":"Unfunded business rates liabilities on investment properties and loss of CATS property revenue.","detail":"The council faces potential business rates liability for the third floor of Suffolk House for six months if the floor remains vacant. The council is also incurring ongoing business rates at Sackville House with rental income below budget. Additionally losing revenue from transfer of CATS properties. Property Investment Strategy forecasts \u00a351k full-year overspend on a \u00a3809k income budget.","category":"other","matters":"Unfunded liabilities on investment properties create budget exposure; rental shortfalls add to cumulative revenue pressures.","figures":"Property Investment Strategy: \u00a3809k budgeted income, \u00a3758k forecast income, \u00a351k forecast overspend","quote":"Sevenoaks District Council could incur business rates for 3rd floor at Suffolk House for six months if floor is vacant. In addition SDC is incurring business rates for Sackville House as well. Council will also lose some revenue from the transfer of CATS (such as The Shambles, Sevenoaks).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","headline":"Bradbourne car park income declining by \u00a360k (10% of annual budget) due to new competing facility opened May 2026.","detail":"Bradbourne car park revenue is significantly underperforming following the opening of a competing Euro Car Park in May 2026. Both day ticket and season ticket income are below budget. Full-year income forecast is \u00a360k below a budgeted income line of \u00a3604k, representing a structural revenue loss unlikely to recover without intervention.","category":"income","matters":"Permanent structural loss of key income stream from market competition; creates revenue pressure requiring compensating savings or increased borrowing.","figures":"Car Parks budgeted income \u00a3604k; forecast income \u00a3544k; actual to date \u00a3551k","quote":"Day tickets income at Bradbourne car park is lower due to new Euro Car Park opened in May 26. Season tickets income below budget.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Consolidated Commentaries - July 26 v2","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68506/68506.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation spending \u00a3149k above budget to date, being managed through reserve draw-down against unfunded government resettlement programme costs.","detail":"Temporary accommodation actual spending reached \u00a3386k against \u00a3237k budgeted to end of July 2026. The council is offsetting this through housing benefit reimbursements, external funding, and draw-down of the TA Reserve. However, these are temporary solutions to an underlying structural demand pressure. The council faces ongoing costs from Government's Homes for Ukraine and Afghan Resettlement schemes while receiving no additional funding. Cost of living and private rented sector changes continue to drive presentations.","category":"demand","matters":"Using reserves to offset unfunded government-mandated demand pressures is not sustainable; the council will face a structural deficit when the reserve is exhausted.","figures":"Temporary accommodation: \u00a3386k actual vs \u00a3237k budget (\u00a3149k variance to date); Rough Sleeping Prevention \u00a373k actual vs \u00a348k budget (\u00a325k overspend); Homelessness Funding grant brought in \u00a3114k actual vs \u00a355k budget","quote":"The Council does not receive additional funding to cover these costs.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Item XX - Treasury Management Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68508/68508.pdf","headline":"A \u00a32.6m loan from Crawley Borough Council matures in June 2026, three months after the report date, requiring immediate refinancing.","detail":"The council has \u00a32.6m due to Crawley Borough Council on 12 June 2026. The loan carries a 4.85% fixed rate. Refinancing will occur in a higher-rate environment than the original loan, and the timing falls just after the Cabinet approval of this report in late September 2026. No prepayment or rescheduling took place in 2025/26.","category":"borrowing","matters":"An imminent maturity within the next quarter creates a defined cash requirement and refinancing event. Current PWLB rates sit at 4.5\u20135.3%, so refinancing cost may be similar or higher than the expiring 4.85% rate, depending on term and credit conditions.","figures":"Crawley Borough Council loan \u00a32,600k maturing 12/06/2026 at 4.85%","quote":"Crawley Borough Council \u00a32.6m Fixed interest payable annually, principal at maturity. 4.85% 3 years to 12/06/2026","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Sevenoaks","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-21","since_iso":"2026-08-22","distress":false,"headline":"The council's budget balance rests entirely on investment income beating expectations.","lead":"A lender depends on understanding whether a council can balance its revenue budget from operations. Councils balancing on elevated investment income face acute vulnerability to rate falls \u2014 and current rates are expected to ease.","also":["20 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-09-22","n_findings":21,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Financial Monitoring to July 26 Appendix B","top_paper_url":"https://sevenoaks.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s68465/68465.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":87,"news_drafts_total":3}}